WEBVTT

00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:08.320
<i>Damn it!</i>

00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:09.080
<i>Turn!</i>

00:00:13.270 --> 00:00:17.870
<i>He's still new and he's the second driver...</i>

00:00:17.870 --> 00:00:20.790
<i>That's why the ace took his car.</i>

00:00:20.790 --> 00:00:21.970
<i>No way.</i>

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:25.080
<i>This is the reality of the pros.</i>

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:29.680
<i>If you want favorable treatment,
 the only thing you can do is get results.</i>

00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:34.770
<i>But how can he get results if they give him a weird car to drive?</i>

00:00:34.770 --> 00:00:36.940
<i>But he still has to do it!</i>

00:00:38.020 --> 00:00:40.330
<i>Like his first win in the kart.</i>

00:00:40.850 --> 00:00:42.900
<i>He has to make the impossible a reality!</i>

00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:48.030
<i>Do your best, Capeta!</i>

00:00:48.030 --> 00:00:51.820
<i>Up until now, you've gone over many walls like this.</i>

00:00:52.880 --> 00:00:55.120
<i>If it's you... you can do it this time, too...</i>

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:06.630
<i>The settings still aren't perfect, but let's think of a way you could drive faster, together.</i>

00:01:07.220 --> 00:01:08.850
<i>Our driving!</i>

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:36.420
<b>All cars have now started!</b>

00:03:36.420 --> 00:03:41.510
<b>The battle for the 6th Formula Stellar race has finally started!</b>

00:03:43.570 --> 00:03:47.610
<b>In the lead is Komazawa from Persec, who started from pole position!</b>

00:03:57.340 --> 00:03:58.390
Damn it!

00:03:58.390 --> 00:04:01.150
<b>Whoa!  It looks like the top has changed!</b>

00:04:01.150 --> 00:04:03.670
<b>It's Ishihara from Sam's, followed by Shiba!</b>

00:04:03.670 --> 00:04:06.490
<b>Komazawa has gone down to 3rd place!</b>

00:04:12.310 --> 00:04:16.520
<b>Falling slightly behind the top group is Taira from Persec, in 4th place!</b>

00:04:18.180 --> 00:04:23.280
<b>Following closely behind him is the attractive female driver, Hata Noriko!</b>

00:04:58.680 --> 00:05:00.290
You're doing great, Ryou!

00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:04.620
Don't lose!

00:05:04.620 --> 00:05:07.210
Go!

00:05:18.420 --> 00:05:20.010
<i>He's driving oddly again.</i>

00:05:33.210 --> 00:05:34.180
Capeta.

00:05:46.800 --> 00:05:49.040
<i>Damn it!  What's with you?!</i>

00:05:49.440 --> 00:05:52.380
<i>If you can't drive decently, hurry up and give way!</i>

00:06:01.100 --> 00:06:03.390
<b>Your time is going down, Noriko.</b>

00:06:03.390 --> 00:06:06.060
<b>It looks like the setting on Taira's machine wasn't thought through well.</b>

00:06:06.060 --> 00:06:07.780
Attack him on the next lap!

00:06:07.780 --> 00:06:08.940
<b>I know!</b>

00:06:16.680 --> 00:06:20.440
Why are the wings of Taira's machine resting?

00:06:22.200 --> 00:06:24.980
With that setting, wouldn't the machine have less grip on the road surface,

00:06:24.980 --> 00:06:27.120
making it harder to turn when it's already difficult enough?

00:06:40.370 --> 00:06:41.470
<i>He has his wings rested.</i>

00:06:51.020 --> 00:06:54.940
<b>Oh no!  Taira from Persec has overrun!</b>

00:06:54.940 --> 00:06:58.440
<b>Three cars have now passed him and he's down to 7th place!</b>

00:07:02.770 --> 00:07:06.410
<b>With this, #3 Hata is up to 4th place!</b>

00:07:03.220 --> 00:07:04.450
All right!

00:07:04.090 --> 00:07:05.480
All right!

00:07:12.050 --> 00:07:15.420
It looked as though he caught a lot of sand, but do you think he's okay?

00:07:15.420 --> 00:07:18.340
I just hope it hasn't gone into the radiator.

00:07:18.340 --> 00:07:21.130
Maybe we made a mistake.

00:07:21.130 --> 00:07:22.650
That's right.

00:07:22.650 --> 00:07:24.080
We have push understeering,

00:07:24.080 --> 00:07:25.830
so even if it means his top speed may fall,

00:07:25.830 --> 00:07:28.520
we should have stood the wings up and pushed the frame downward.

00:07:28.970 --> 00:07:29.970
Yeah.

00:07:29.970 --> 00:07:31.940
But he thought of the opposite.

00:07:32.480 --> 00:07:33.270
The opposite?

00:07:33.730 --> 00:07:36.070
Huh?  What does that mean?

00:07:36.070 --> 00:07:40.530
Rather than trying hard to force something that doesn't turn,

00:07:40.530 --> 00:07:44.790
Capeta thought it was better to enhance the top speed.

00:07:53.160 --> 00:07:55.000
So... in other words...

00:07:55.710 --> 00:07:58.500
Rather than adjusting the machine in his favor,

00:07:58.500 --> 00:08:02.280
he's trying to adjust his driving to the special characteristics of the machine.

00:08:02.280 --> 00:08:03.430
That's it, right?

00:08:03.430 --> 00:08:04.360
Yeah.

00:08:04.360 --> 00:08:06.480
Capeta always did it that way.

00:08:06.480 --> 00:08:09.870
No matter whether his machine was inferior or he had some sort of handicap,

00:08:09.870 --> 00:08:12.520
he could drive using those to his advantage.

00:08:15.400 --> 00:08:16.740
<i>Okay.</i>

00:08:16.740 --> 00:08:18.450
<i>I'm starting to get it.</i>

00:08:39.500 --> 00:08:42.590
Go!  Go!

00:08:41.510 --> 00:08:42.590
Capeta!

00:08:42.590 --> 00:08:44.660
<b>Whoa!  Taira makes a move!</b>

00:08:44.660 --> 00:08:46.510
<b>But he got blocked!</b>

00:08:46.510 --> 00:08:47.980
<b>He tries again from the outside!</b>

00:08:47.980 --> 00:08:50.010
<b>Taira's top speed is better!</b>

00:08:50.010 --> 00:08:52.330
<b>But this is overspeeding!</b>

00:08:52.980 --> 00:08:54.440
Capeta!

00:09:02.570 --> 00:09:03.610
<b>He passed!</b>

00:09:03.610 --> 00:09:05.290
<b>Car #63, Taira!</b>

00:09:05.290 --> 00:09:06.950
<b>He's up to 6th place!</b>

00:09:06.950 --> 00:09:07.960
All right!

00:09:07.960 --> 00:09:09.370
All right!!

00:09:09.370 --> 00:09:12.870
He did it!!

00:09:13.880 --> 00:09:15.130
That's right!

00:09:15.130 --> 00:09:22.500
Even on his first time with the kart, when he got the course record, and at Haruna in the hard rain...

00:09:22.500 --> 00:09:27.060
As long as Capeta gets the hang of the machine...

00:09:27.060 --> 00:09:29.000
He won't lose to anyone!

00:09:30.440 --> 00:09:31.560
All right!

00:09:31.560 --> 00:09:33.310
Go for it, kid!

00:09:33.310 --> 00:09:35.710
<b>Oh, is Taira going to dive in by force?!</b>

00:09:35.710 --> 00:09:36.640
<b>Can he make it?!</b>

00:09:36.640 --> 00:09:38.560
<b>Yes!  He passed!</b>

00:09:41.230 --> 00:09:46.340
<b>A-Although he's a newcomer, he's showing an incredible chase!</b>

00:09:46.340 --> 00:09:47.450
<b>He's up to 5th place!</b>

00:09:47.450 --> 00:09:48.670
All right!

00:09:48.670 --> 00:09:49.700
Capeta!

00:09:49.700 --> 00:09:52.660
Go!

00:09:54.620 --> 00:09:55.600
Who is he?

00:09:55.600 --> 00:09:57.250
#63?

00:09:57.250 --> 00:09:58.240
Is that it?

00:09:58.240 --> 00:09:59.580
What's going on?

00:10:06.090 --> 00:10:07.660
Capeta!

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:11.550
All right, Ryou!

00:10:32.410 --> 00:10:33.220
<b>Noriko!</b>

00:10:33.220 --> 00:10:35.060
<b>Taira is coming, 2 seconds behind you!</b>

00:10:35.060 --> 00:10:36.000
<b>Don't let your guard down!</b>

00:10:36.650 --> 00:10:38.000
H-How?!

00:10:40.380 --> 00:10:41.260
<i>Taira...</i>

00:10:42.180 --> 00:10:44.390
<i>I won't lose to you this time.</i>

00:10:48.030 --> 00:10:52.970
<b>We've now reached the middle of the race,
 entering the 6th lap out of 15!</b>

00:10:52.970 --> 00:10:56.140
<b>The one to watch is the fierce battle for 4th place!</b>

00:10:56.140 --> 00:10:59.140
Go, Capeta!

00:11:14.730 --> 00:11:16.160
<i>Just a bit more!</i>

00:11:25.040 --> 00:11:27.300
<i>H-How?!</i>

00:11:27.300 --> 00:11:28.840
<i>There was such a big gap!</i>

00:11:29.610 --> 00:11:31.060
<i>How did he?!</i>

00:11:31.060 --> 00:11:33.180
<i>With messed up driving like that?!</i>

00:11:47.030 --> 00:11:48.640
Taira's gone!

00:11:48.640 --> 00:11:50.330
Where did he go?!

00:11:50.330 --> 00:11:51.160
<b>Noriko!</b>

00:11:51.160 --> 00:11:52.400
<b>He's right behind you!</b>

00:11:57.120 --> 00:12:00.980
<b>Whoa!  Taira closely follows inside Hata's slipstream!</b>

00:12:00.980 --> 00:12:03.080
<b>This is fierce nose-to-tail racing!</b>

00:12:07.460 --> 00:12:09.920
<b>Can Hata shake him off?!</b>

00:12:12.300 --> 00:12:13.140
I can't get him off!

00:12:37.740 --> 00:12:40.260
<b>Whoa!  The one who passed is Taira!</b>

00:12:40.260 --> 00:12:44.040
<b>He overtook #3 Hata and is now in 4th place!</b>

00:12:44.040 --> 00:12:46.000
All right!

00:12:49.420 --> 00:12:53.150
C-Capeta!  You're so great!

00:12:53.150 --> 00:12:56.030
Shige!  It's too early to be crying!

00:12:55.640 --> 00:12:56.680
All right!

00:13:03.160 --> 00:13:05.760
That courage.  That fighting spirit.

00:13:05.760 --> 00:13:07.280
It's not just his techniques.

00:13:07.280 --> 00:13:12.150
Taira is also leveling up in spirit.

00:13:12.710 --> 00:13:16.610
A strong will that's necessary in a great driver.

00:13:16.610 --> 00:13:20.200
Not just for overcoming rivals, but yourself as well...

00:13:20.750 --> 00:13:23.550
The tough days on the kart...

00:13:24.610 --> 00:13:26.770
have helped him to shine.

00:13:27.680 --> 00:13:31.090
Those tough days made Taira.

00:13:32.880 --> 00:13:37.280
<b>Oh no!  We have an engine blow in front of the last corner!</b>

00:13:43.580 --> 00:13:44.670
It's hot.

00:13:45.670 --> 00:13:49.700
It's still the beginning of July and it's not even rain season.

00:13:49.700 --> 00:13:51.480
But this is like the heat of high summer.

00:14:00.460 --> 00:14:03.070
It's true that it's hard on the drivers,

00:14:03.690 --> 00:14:07.410
but with this heat, it's also hard on the machine.

00:14:07.900 --> 00:14:09.140
Engine...  Tires...  Brakes...

00:14:09.140 --> 00:14:10.370
Engine...  Tires...  Brakes...

00:14:10.370 --> 00:14:11.860
Engine...  Tires...  Brakes...

00:14:11.860 --> 00:14:14.280
Their temperature becomes extremely high.

00:14:14.280 --> 00:14:17.380
It's because they're already hot that the extra heat becomes a burden.

00:14:18.010 --> 00:14:19.100
That's right.

00:14:19.700 --> 00:14:24.710
From here on it'll be a battle of how good you care for your machine and lead it to the goal.

00:14:25.430 --> 00:14:28.270
He may not be able to survive just by speed.

00:14:36.650 --> 00:14:39.300
<b>In this heat wave of over 30°C,</b>

00:14:39.300 --> 00:14:44.380
<b>some of the machines are starting to have engine and tire troubles, and some cars are even retiring.</b>

00:14:45.240 --> 00:14:50.820
<b>In the midst of it all, with Sam's one-two formation, we are entering the 8th lap!</b>

00:14:50.820 --> 00:14:54.820
<b>Closely following them is Persec's Komazawa, followed by Taira!</b>

00:14:59.970 --> 00:15:01.150
<i>What?!</i>

00:15:01.150 --> 00:15:03.050
<i>There's 2 seconds between me and Taira?</i>

00:15:04.480 --> 00:15:06.240
<i>That sounds fun.</i>

00:15:06.240 --> 00:15:09.560
<i>Follow me if you can, Taira!</i>

00:15:13.530 --> 00:15:15.420
What should we do, Tsubomaki-san?

00:15:15.420 --> 00:15:18.800
Capeta's lap time is more than
 1 second faster than Komazawa's.

00:15:18.800 --> 00:15:24.000
He'll probably catch up to him in no time, but should we order him to stand his position?

00:15:30.390 --> 00:15:35.960
<b>Oh?  From the looks of it, the top group is having trouble passing a back marker.</b>

00:15:40.430 --> 00:15:42.250
<i>What are you doing?!</i>

00:15:42.250 --> 00:15:43.390
<i>Hurry up and let me pass!</i>

00:15:55.650 --> 00:15:57.800
Go, Taira!

00:16:05.620 --> 00:16:06.980
Taira!

00:16:05.620 --> 00:16:07.630
That's it!  Go!

00:16:07.630 --> 00:16:08.890
Pass them!

00:16:08.390 --> 00:16:09.480
You're so cool!

00:16:09.480 --> 00:16:10.550
Taira!

00:16:10.550 --> 00:16:11.130
Go!

00:16:11.130 --> 00:16:13.020
Taira!  You're giving me shivers!

00:16:13.020 --> 00:16:14.710
Taira!  Where are you?!

00:16:13.800 --> 00:16:15.630
He sure is popular.

00:16:20.730 --> 00:16:22.630
<i>So you're here, Capeta!</i>

00:16:31.760 --> 00:16:33.310
It's fighting spirit!

00:16:45.080 --> 00:16:48.100
<i>To think you could fight this much in your first race.</i>

00:16:48.100 --> 00:16:50.350
<i>To be honest I didn't think you could...</i>

00:16:50.350 --> 00:16:53.130
<i>with that spare car that doesn't turn properly.</i>

00:16:59.540 --> 00:17:01.080
<i>Come to think of it,</i>

00:17:01.080 --> 00:17:04.330
<i>they said that after he crashed in the mock race at FSRS,</i>

00:17:04.330 --> 00:17:09.290
<i>he continued to drive at the same speed and dove into the corners on the same line.</i>

00:17:12.250 --> 00:17:15.920
<i>I made fun of all the students from that school and thought they were all softies,</i>

00:17:15.920 --> 00:17:18.270
<i>but you're not like that.</i>

00:17:19.950 --> 00:17:20.780
<i>No.</i>

00:17:20.780 --> 00:17:22.240
<i>It's not just Capeta.</i>

00:17:22.240 --> 00:17:24.570
<i>I keep falling behind those two at the front too.</i>

00:17:25.680 --> 00:17:27.070
<i>This is a disgrace.</i>

00:17:31.580 --> 00:17:36.870
<i>And even when I got you to hand over your machine and swore I'd win this race.</i>

00:17:39.380 --> 00:17:41.530
<i>But I have pride too.</i>

00:17:41.530 --> 00:17:46.840
<i>As the ace of this team,
I can't lose to you no matter what!</i>

00:17:48.430 --> 00:17:53.100
<b>Now at the back of the control line,
 Taira bites at Komazawa!</b>

00:17:53.480 --> 00:17:56.310
Go, Taira!

00:18:10.090 --> 00:18:13.980
<i>I'm sorry, Tsubomaki-san, but who cares about prioritizing by fighting strength.</i>

00:18:13.980 --> 00:18:16.120
<i>All I want to do is race!</i>

00:18:16.670 --> 00:18:18.670
<b>Taira finally attacks from inside!</b>

00:18:18.670 --> 00:18:20.990
<b>Komazawa also quickly blocks!</b>

00:18:21.910 --> 00:18:23.630
<b>Oh!  He goes from the inside again!</b>

00:18:23.630 --> 00:18:25.550
<i>Like I'd lose!</i>

00:18:27.510 --> 00:18:29.190
<i>I can still go!</i>

00:18:29.190 --> 00:18:31.180
<i>It's fighting spirit!</i>

00:18:41.220 --> 00:18:42.820
Komazawa!

00:18:43.170 --> 00:18:45.610
<b>Oh!  Komazawa falls down to 4th place!</b>

00:18:45.610 --> 00:18:47.690
<b>With this, Taira is finally in 3rd place!</b>

00:18:54.420 --> 00:18:55.710
<i>Go, Capeta.</i>

00:18:56.230 --> 00:18:58.790
<i>You go on ahead.</i>

00:18:59.660 --> 00:19:03.750
<i>I'll hold back all those behind us.</i>

00:19:04.480 --> 00:19:06.710
Capeta is in 3rd place.

00:19:06.710 --> 00:19:08.200
That's right.

00:19:08.200 --> 00:19:11.930
Capeta is fighting well in my place.

00:19:11.930 --> 00:19:13.080
Yeah.

00:19:13.080 --> 00:19:16.430
Capeta is fighting far better than we expected.

00:19:17.070 --> 00:19:21.940
If you drive like this in your debut race,
 no one can ignore you.

00:19:23.800 --> 00:19:24.440
Yes.

00:19:24.440 --> 00:19:25.970
<b>It's not "yes"!</b>

00:19:25.970 --> 00:19:28.280
<b>Why haven't you called me?!</b>

00:19:28.730 --> 00:19:29.900
<b>Monami?!</b>

00:19:29.900 --> 00:19:32.780
I'm heading that way quickly right now.

00:19:33.640 --> 00:19:35.260
<b>So how's Ca-chan doing?</b>

00:19:35.260 --> 00:19:36.330
Don't be surprised.

00:19:36.330 --> 00:19:37.260
He's in 3rd place!

00:19:37.260 --> 00:19:38.640
Amazing, isn't it?

00:19:38.640 --> 00:19:40.490
<b>Don't be kidding me!</b>

00:19:40.490 --> 00:19:42.790
<b>3rd is the same as losing!</b>

00:19:42.790 --> 00:19:45.060
<b>There's no point if he doesn't win!</b>

00:19:46.960 --> 00:19:48.560
Really.

00:19:48.560 --> 00:19:51.800
It doesn't look like they have the spirit to fight if I'm not around, so please hurry.

00:19:51.800 --> 00:19:53.100
Okay.

00:19:57.660 --> 00:20:00.990
<b>There are only 5 laps to go now!</b>

00:20:01.640 --> 00:20:04.000
<b>The top is Ishihara from Sam's.</b>

00:20:04.000 --> 00:20:05.740
<b>He's in a one-two formation with Shiba.</b>

00:20:05.740 --> 00:20:09.830
<b>And behind them, the center of our attention, 16-year-old Taira,</b>

00:20:09.830 --> 00:20:12.070
<b>has shortened his time between them by 1.5 seconds!</b>

00:20:12.070 --> 00:20:13.650
All right!

00:20:13.650 --> 00:20:14.940
Capeta!

00:20:24.810 --> 00:20:27.100
There's something wrong with the sound of the engine!

00:20:27.100 --> 00:20:27.920
Capeta's?

00:20:31.060 --> 00:20:32.720
It's this heat.

00:20:32.720 --> 00:20:34.380
It's probably the radiator.

00:20:35.310 --> 00:20:36.650
The radiator!

00:20:36.650 --> 00:20:38.890
Come to think of it, on his 2nd lap...

00:20:41.680 --> 00:20:44.320
Sand must have gotten into the radiator then.

00:20:44.320 --> 00:20:45.080
Taira!

00:20:45.080 --> 00:20:46.610
Is there anything wrong with the water temperature?!

00:20:49.280 --> 00:20:51.030
<b>Hey.  Answer me.</b>

00:20:51.030 --> 00:20:52.110
<b>Taira!</b>

00:20:52.110 --> 00:20:53.910
Can't you hear me?!

00:20:53.910 --> 00:20:55.700
Taira!

00:21:03.740 --> 00:21:05.770
<b>Check the water temperature!</b>

00:21:05.770 --> 00:21:06.850
<b>Taira!</b>

00:22:50.880 --> 00:22:52.650
The rays of the sun and the heat of the road surface...

00:22:52.650 --> 00:22:55.610
It wouldn't be strange if Capeta's machine were to break down at any time.

00:22:55.960 --> 00:22:58.450
But he'll never give up!

00:22:58.450 --> 00:23:00.650
He'll fight until the very end!

00:23:00.650 --> 00:23:01.910
Final episode of Capeta.

00:23:01.910 --> 00:23:03.080
Checkered Flag!

00:23:03.440 --> 00:23:05.940
Open up the future!
